  "worked_solution": "Let $BC=x.$\n\nSince the perimeter of the rectangle is $p=32$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =AB+BC+CD+DA \\\\ p & =2(AB)+2(BC) \\\\ 32 & =2(3x)+2(x) \\\\ 32 & =6x+2x \\\\ 8x & =32 \\\\ x & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain $BC=4$ and $AB=3\\cdot 4=12.$\n\nTherefore, the area of a rectangle $ABCD$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =12\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
